   "note": "The task is graph connectivity, which is invariant under node relabeling (permutation symmetry). To exploit this, the ansatz block is designed to be equivariant under cyclic permutations of the qubits (representing nodes). The block consists of uniform single-qubit rotations (RY, RZ) followed by a ring of CNOTs (0-1, 1-2, ..., 5-0). This structure ensures that if the input feature map respects the symmetry (which it should, as graph features are symmetric), the circuit evolution preserves the permutation symmetry. The tied parameters (theta_i, phi_i) enforce uniformity across sites. The CNOT ring allows information to propagate across the graph, enabling the detection of connectivity components. The readout uses pairwise Z_iZ_j observables, which are also permutation invariant. This design reduces the parameter space to 12 parameters (2 per qubit) while maintaining high expressivity for graph properties, likely improving generalization over asymmetric ansatzes like c0004 or c0005.",
